    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2021-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We can express this expression in base \\(10\\) using the definition of bases: \\[ 2b^3 + 2b + 1 - 2b^2 - 2b - 1 \\]\\[= 2b^3 - 2b^2 = 2b^2(b - 1). \\]\n\nFor this to be divisible by \\(3,\\) either \\(b\\) or \\(b - 1\\) must be divisible by \\(3.\\)\n\nThe only answer choice that satisfies neither of these conditions is \\(8.\\)\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Convert \\(2021_b-221_b\\) to base \\(10\\)",
        "Check when \\(2b^2(b-1)\\) is divisible by \\(3\\)"
      ],
